1.02.363.597 D slot launch_slot_: id  0 | task -1 | launching slot : {"id":0,"n_ctx":25088,"speculative":false,"is_processing":false,"id_task":0,"n_prompt_tokens":12295,"n_prompt_tokens_processed":0,"n_prompt_tokens_cache":0,"params":{"seed":910272,"temperature":0.699999988079071,"dynatemp_range":0.0,"dynatemp_exponent":1.0,"top_k":20,"top_p":0.800000011920929,"min_p":0.0,"top_n_sigma":-1.0,"xtc_probability":0.0,"xtc_threshold":0.10000000149011612,"typical_p":1.0,"repeat_last_n":64,"repeat_penalty":1.0,"presence_penalty":1.5,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"dry_multiplier":0.0,"dry_base":1.75,"dry_allowed_length":2,"dry_penalty_last_n":64,"dry_sequence_breakers":["\n",":","\"","*"],"mirostat":0,"mirostat_tau":5.0,"mirostat_eta":0.10000000149011612,"adaptive_target":-1.0,"adaptive_decay":0.8999999761581421,"stop":[],"max_tokens":2700,"n_predict":2700,"n_keep":0,"n_discard":0,"ignore_eos":false,"stream":false,"logit_bias":[],"n_probs":0,"min_keep":0,"grammar":"","grammar_lazy":false,"grammar_triggers":[],"preserved_tokens":[248058,248059,248068,248069],"chat_format":"peg-native","reasoning_format":"deepseek","reasoning_in_content":false,"generation_prompt":"<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","samplers":["penalties","dry","top_n_sigma","top_k","typ_p","top_p","min_p","xtc","temperature"],"speculative.types":"none","timings_per_token":false,"post_sampling_probs":false,"backend_sampling":false,"lora":[]},"next_token":[{"has_next_token":false,"has_new_line":false,"n_remain":-1,"n_decoded":0}],"prompt":"<|im_start|>system\n# BATCHED_EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION maintenance mode\n\nReturn only a complete replacement Markdown evidence-integration ledger whose\nfirst line is exactly `# Evidence Integration Ledger`. Do not take an ordinary task\naction. Integrate the exact batch with the prior task work, preserving units,\nprobabilities, revisions, qualifications, contradictions, cross-source\nrelationships, R01-R12 bindings, and unresolved blockers.\n\nThe output is model-authored and lossy. It cannot authorize readiness or\nsubmission. Replace prior material rather than appending indefinitely. Keep it\nunder the hard 2400-token limit. The only source IDs you\nmay cite are: S01, S02, S03, S04, S05, S06.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Authoritative task\n\n# Task: Bluehaven drinking-water restoration package\n\nA river contamination event, power instability, and distribution constraints\nthreaten Bluehaven's drinking-water system. Produce two exact deliverables:\n\n1. `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md`\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`\n\nThe fixed second filename is imposed by the runtime; its content is an\noperational drinking-water restoration decision. Reconcile the complete system\nover seventy-two hours rather than summarizing sources independently.\n\n## Evidence-ledger contract\n\nBegin with `# Evidence Integration Ledger` and maintain entries `R01` through\n`R12`. Each entry must state a disposition, cite only exact observed sources as\n`[SNN]`, preserve units, probabilities, revisions, conflicts and\nqualifications, bind current or missing evidence, and name blockers. The ledger\nis model-authored, lossy task work and never readiness authority.\n\n## Decision-document contract\n\nBegin with `# Bluehaven Drinking-Water Restoration Decision` and use exactly\nthese level-two headings in this order:\n\n1. `## Decision, scope, and authority`\n2. `## Contamination triggers and service-zone sequencing`\n3. `## Demand, treatment, and distribution capacity`\n4. `## Critical customers and alternate-water continuity`\n5. `## Power, staffing, logistics, and mutual aid`\n6. `## Public warning, sampling, and accountability`\n7. `## Seventy-two-hour execution and contingencies`\n8. `## Verification, readiness, blockers, and falsifiers`\n\nWrite 1,400–2,000 words excluding exact citations. Cite at least twelve unique\nsources and include S01–S11 and S13–S16.\n\nResolve these coupled requirements:\n\n- `R01`: recommendation, public-health order, operations, checking, handoff,\n  cost escalation, and closure authority;\n- `R02`: exact residual and benzene triggers, conservative plume branch,\n  hold/lift observations, expiry, and common forecast/sample/action binding;\n- `R03`: population and time-bound potable demand, overlapping vulnerability,\n  registry coverage, uncovered-population uncertainty, loss, and critical demand;\n- `R04`: shared East-trunk treatment limit, observed output, hydraulic delivery,\n  pressure, valve/pump effects, and current capacity proof;\n- `R05`: hospitals, dialysis, care facilities, accessible/private matching,\n  potable specifications, handoffs, and blocking thresholds;\n- `R06`: certified tanker and bottle capacity, staffed cycles, activation,\n  disinfection, shared loading assets, road/vendor constraints, and relief;\n- `R07`: generator endurance, observed fuel delay, local staging or alternate\n  supply, laboratory power, staffing qualifications, duty, and safety;\n- `R08`: multilingual redundant warning, outage-aware reach, door-knock time,\n  exact revision, receipt/understanding evidence, and correction;\n- `R09`: sample locations, custody, quality control, six/nine-hour assays, two\n  clean rounds, candidate currency, and release authority;\n- `R10`: private accountability, public aggregation, verified self-supply,\n  restricted clinical data, reconciliation, seven/thirty-day retention, and\n  deletion proof;\n- `R11`: executable seventy-two-hour sequence with owners, resources, effects,\n  current checks, repair, recheck, cost authority, and contingencies; and\n- `R12`: every exercise and independent-review blocker, source uncertainty,\n  candidate-bound readiness, explicit falsifiers, and correct closure.\n\nPreserve source distinctions exactly. In particular, do not convert a\nchemical threshold into a duration or flow, a forecast probability into a\nphysical measurement or demand estimate, registry coverage into demand\nreduction, a shared bottleneck into summed capacity, a common revision binding\ninto a count of permitted changes, or a contractual target into observed\nperformance. Recover the exact values and qualifications from the source\nrecord rather than treating this task statement as evidence.\n\nAlso preserve that:\n\n- owner attestation, component dashboards, stale checks, ledgers, and\n  submission are not readiness proof.\n\n\n# Prior accepted integration ledger\n\n# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\nNo accepted evidence has been integrated yet.\n\n# Mechanically batched exact externalized observations\n\n## Externalized exact result RESULT-001\n\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:S01:1-70+S02:1-70\",\"object_version\":\"6ead1f44b5f6c472ff68cda7d53c92ed8aa4c5eca9ad213830ab81c5fc8cd6bb\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S02\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8341}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S01_AUTHORITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"c90f647766613d6e81f7cb2f7a2738bf3119e90ca8385ba3b2d7b9fadc4f7685\",\"source_size_bytes\":4182,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Bluehaven emergency drinking-water authority\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe public-health officer issues or lifts a boil-water order after the utility laboratory recommendation. The utility director owns operational restoration; neither a vendor nor a dashboard can declare public-health readiness.\nThe operations chief may isolate mains and dispatch tankers, while the mayor controls emergency expenditure above the utility director's delegated ceiling. These roles are distinct.\nA shift handoff is valid only when the receiving officer acknowledges the same incident-plan and water-quality revision. An unacknowledged transfer blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nTrigger evidence from S02 and S15 informs the health officer but does not replace the legal order. Restoration effects require a current laboratory and hydraulic check.\nEvery public notice, field action, and checker must bind the same incident revision and effective time.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUTH-000 | utility-director | r2 | 1.0 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-001 | health-officer | r2 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-002 | operations-chief | r2 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-003 | mayor | r2 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-004 | utility-director | r2 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-005 | health-officer | r2 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-006 | operations-chief | r2 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-007 | mayor | r2 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-008 | utility-director | r2 | 3.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-009 | health-officer | r2 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-010 | operations-chief | r2 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-011 | mayor | r2 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-012 | utility-director | r2 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-013 | health-officer | r2 | 3.9 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-014 | operations-chief | r2 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-015 | mayor | r2 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-016 | utility-director | r3 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-017 | health-officer | r3 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-018 | operations-chief | r3 | 1.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-019 | mayor | r3 | 1.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-020 | utility-director | r3 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-021 | health-officer | r3 | 3.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-022 | operations-chief | r3 | 4.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-023 | mayor | r3 | 1.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-024 | utility-director | r3 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-025 | health-officer | r3 | 3.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-026 | operations-chief | r3 | 3.7 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-027 | mayor | r3 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-028 | utility-director | r3 | 2.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-029 | health-officer | r3 | 2.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-030 | operations-chief | r3 | 3.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-031 | mayor | r3 | 1.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-032 | utility-director | r4 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-033 | health-officer | r4 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-034 | operations-chief | r4 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-035 | mayor | r4 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-036 | utility-director | r4 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-037 | health-officer | r4 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-038 | operations-chief | r4 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-039 | mayor | r4 | 3.5 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-040 | utility-director | r4 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-041 | health-officer | r4 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-042 | operations-chief | r4 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-043 | mayor | r4 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-044 | utility-director | r4 | 3.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-045 | health-officer | r4 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-046 | operations-chief | r4 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-047 | mayor | r4 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nDistinguish recommendation, legal order, operational execution, verification, and closure authority.\nDo not treat a model-authored ledger, vendor assertion, or submission as readiness authority.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S02\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S02_CONTAMINATION.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"2271ec6007702903ad1c4dcecd819c4ec176e7345a0323c2bbe47e00954ade0c\",\"source_size_bytes\":3707,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Contamination thresholds and conservative response triggers\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nA mandatory boil-water order begins when treated chlorine residual remains below 0.2 mg/L in two consecutive validated samples or when benzene exceeds 5 micrograms per liter in any confirmed distribution sample.\nThe median plume forecast stays north of the intake, but 38 percent of current ensemble members reverse after 18:00. The conservative branch governs intake isolation until field samples rule it out.\nOne clean sample cannot cancel an active order. Lifting requires two compliant rounds, hydraulic stabilization, and public-health approval.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nDemand and alternate-water supply from S03 and S08 must cover the period implied by laboratory turnaround in S09, not only pipe travel time.\nRiver forecast revision in S15, treatment state in S04, and public notice in S10 must remain on one candidate-bound revision.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| WQ-000 | North-intake | r2 | 0.2 | mg/L | hold |\n| WQ-001 | East-clearwell | r2 | 0.9 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-002 | Zone-A | r2 | 1.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-003 | Zone-B | r2 | 2.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-004 | North-intake | r2 | 3.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-005 | East-clearwell | r2 | 0.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-006 | Zone-A | r2 | 1.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-007 | Zone-B | r2 | 2.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-008 | North-intake | r2 | 2.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-009 | East-clearwell | r2 | 0.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-010 | Zone-A | r2 | 1.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-011 | Zone-B | r2 | 1.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-012 | North-intake | r2 | 2.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-013 | East-clearwell | r2 | 3.1 | mg/L | hold |\n| WQ-014 | Zone-A | r2 | 0.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-015 | Zone-B | r2 | 1.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-016 | North-intake | r3 | 2.1 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-017 | East-clearwell | r3 | 2.8 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-018 | Zone-A | r3 | 0.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-019 | Zone-B | r3 | 1.1 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-020 | North-intake | r3 | 1.8 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-021 | East-clearwell | r3 | 2.5 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-022 | Zone-A | r3 | 3.2 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-023 | Zone-B | r3 | 0.8 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-024 | North-intake | r3 | 1.5 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-025 | East-clearwell | r3 | 2.2 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-026 | Zone-A | r3 | 2.9 | mg/L | hold |\n| WQ-027 | Zone-B | r3 | 0.5 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-028 | North-intake | r3 | 1.2 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-029 | East-clearwell | r3 | 1.9 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-030 | Zone-A | r3 | 2.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-031 | Zone-B | r3 | 0.2 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-032 | North-intake | r4 | 0.9 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-033 | East-clearwell | r4 | 1.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-034 | Zone-A | r4 | 2.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-035 | Zone-B | r4 | 3.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-036 | North-intake | r4 | 0.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-037 | East-clearwell | r4 | 1.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-038 | Zone-A | r4 | 2.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-039 | Zone-B | r4 | 2.7 | mg/L | hold |\n| WQ-040 | North-intake | r4 | 0.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-041 | East-clearwell | r4 | 1.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-042 | Zone-A | r4 | 1.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-043 | Zone-B | r4 | 2.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-044 | North-intake | r4 | 3.1 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-045 | East-clearwell | r4 | 0.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-046 | Zone-A | r4 | 1.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-047 | Zone-B | r4 | 2.1 | mg/L | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve 0.2 mg/L, 5 micrograms per liter, and 38 percent with their exact meanings and units.\nState the observations that start, hold, expand, and lift each protective action.\n\n## Externalized exact result RESULT-002\n\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:S03:1-70+S04:1-70\",\"object_version\":\"55d17ff7177afbe97753425481cc305623d764d31a0c72fecb1db120c87f8ce2\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S03\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S04\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8691}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S03\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S03_DEMAND.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"542346c71ea244ed887ad9fa9e4901722fdfc2f67cd629cec2503f4f964f30b5\",\"source_size_bytes\":4204,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Service-zone demand, registry coverage, and vulnerable households\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nBluehaven serves 46,800 residents: 8,200 in Zone A, 12,600 in B, 15,400 in C, and 10,600 in D. Daytime industrial demand adds 2.4 megaliters per day but is not drinking-water demand.\nThe emergency minimum is three liters per person per day plus separately calculated clinical and sanitation demand. Vulnerability categories overlap and cannot be summed as independent people.\nThe customer and meter registry covers 94 percent of occupied premises. The uncovered six percent requires an uncertainty allowance; it is not a six-percent reduction in demand.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nTreatment and distribution capacity in S04-S05 must be compared with time-bound potable demand after losses, not with nominal plant nameplate totals.\nCritical facilities in S07 and tanker logistics in S08 need explicit priority allocations outside the household minimum.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| DEM-000 | Zone-A | r2 | 46.8 | thousand-people | hold |\n| DEM-001 | Zone-B | r2 | 47.5 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-002 | Zone-C | r2 | 48.2 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-003 | Zone-D | r2 | 48.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-004 | Zone-A | r2 | 49.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-005 | Zone-B | r2 | 47.2 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-006 | Zone-C | r2 | 47.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-007 | Zone-D | r2 | 48.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-008 | Zone-A | r2 | 49.3 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-009 | Zone-B | r2 | 46.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-010 | Zone-C | r2 | 47.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-011 | Zone-D | r2 | 48.3 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-012 | Zone-A | r2 | 49.0 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-013 | Zone-B | r2 | 49.7 | thousand-people | hold |\n| DEM-014 | Zone-C | r2 | 47.3 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-015 | Zone-D | r2 | 48.0 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-016 | Zone-A | r3 | 48.7 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-017 | Zone-B | r3 | 49.4 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-018 | Zone-C | r3 | 47.0 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-019 | Zone-D | r3 | 47.7 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-020 | Zone-A | r3 | 48.4 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-021 | Zone-B | r3 | 49.1 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-022 | Zone-C | r3 | 49.8 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-023 | Zone-D | r3 | 47.4 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-024 | Zone-A | r3 | 48.1 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-025 | Zone-B | r3 | 48.8 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-026 | Zone-C | r3 | 49.5 | thousand-people | hold |\n| DEM-027 | Zone-D | r3 | 47.1 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-028 | Zone-A | r3 | 47.8 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-029 | Zone-B | r3 | 48.5 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-030 | Zone-C | r3 | 49.2 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-031 | Zone-D | r3 | 46.8 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-032 | Zone-A | r4 | 47.5 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-033 | Zone-B | r4 | 48.2 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-034 | Zone-C | r4 | 48.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-035 | Zone-D | r4 | 49.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-036 | Zone-A | r4 | 47.2 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-037 | Zone-B | r4 | 47.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-038 | Zone-C | r4 | 48.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-039 | Zone-D | r4 | 49.3 | thousand-people | hold |\n| DEM-040 | Zone-A | r4 | 46.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-041 | Zone-B | r4 | 47.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-042 | Zone-C | r4 | 48.3 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-043 | Zone-D | r4 | 49.0 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-044 | Zone-A | r4 | 49.7 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-045 | Zone-B | r4 | 47.3 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-046 | Zone-C | r4 | 48.0 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-047 | Zone-D | r4 | 48.7 | thousand-people | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nState population basis, overlap rule, registry uncertainty, loss allowance, and time-bound demand.\nDo not convert 94 percent coverage into a 94 percent readiness score or six percent into a demand target.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S04\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S04_TREATMENT.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"31775314f25121b2200159075bc3c4035b479973fad09eb9b60ac8d8ca604e41\",\"source_size_bytes\":4042,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Treatment-plant capacity and shared clearwell limits\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nPlant A is rated at 12 megaliters per day and Plant B at 9, but both discharge through the East clearwell and trunk whose validated sustainable limit is 15 megaliters per day. The ratings cannot be added to claim 21.\nThe last integrated run sustained 13.4 megaliters per day after filter backwash and distribution losses. A higher figure requires a current candidate-bound test.\nPlant B cannot treat the benzene branch without the mobile carbon unit, whose activation and staffing are governed by S12.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nHydraulic zone pressure in S05 can reduce deliverable potable capacity below treatment output. Generator state in S06 constrains both plants and the shared clearwell pumps.\nAlternate-water obligations in S08 are the gap between validated delivered capacity and demand, not the gap from nameplate output.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| PLANT-000 | Plant-A | r2 | 13.4 | ML/day | hold |\n| PLANT-001 | Plant-B | r2 | 14.1 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-002 | East-clearwell | r2 | 14.8 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-003 | West-clearwell | r2 | 15.5 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-004 | Plant-A | r2 | 16.2 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-005 | Plant-B | r2 | 13.8 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-006 | East-clearwell | r2 | 14.5 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-007 | West-clearwell | r2 | 15.2 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-008 | Plant-A | r2 | 15.9 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-009 | Plant-B | r2 | 13.5 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-010 | East-clearwell | r2 | 14.2 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-011 | West-clearwell | r2 | 14.9 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-012 | Plant-A | r2 | 15.6 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-013 | Plant-B | r2 | 16.3 | ML/day | hold |\n| PLANT-014 | East-clearwell | r2 | 13.9 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-015 | West-clearwell | r2 | 14.6 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-016 | Plant-A | r3 | 15.3 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-017 | Plant-B | r3 | 16.0 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-018 | East-clearwell | r3 | 13.6 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-019 | West-clearwell | r3 | 14.3 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-020 | Plant-A | r3 | 15.0 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-021 | Plant-B | r3 | 15.7 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-022 | East-clearwell | r3 | 16.4 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-023 | West-clearwell | r3 | 14.0 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-024 | Plant-A | r3 | 14.7 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-025 | Plant-B | r3 | 15.4 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-026 | East-clearwell | r3 | 16.1 | ML/day | hold |\n| PLANT-027 | West-clearwell | r3 | 13.7 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-028 | Plant-A | r3 | 14.4 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-029 | Plant-B | r3 | 15.1 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-030 | East-clearwell | r3 | 15.8 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-031 | West-clearwell | r3 | 13.4 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-032 | Plant-A | r4 | 14.1 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-033 | Plant-B | r4 | 14.8 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-034 | East-clearwell | r4 | 15.5 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-035 | West-clearwell | r4 | 16.2 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-036 | Plant-A | r4 | 13.8 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-037 | Plant-B | r4 | 14.5 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-038 | East-clearwell | r4 | 15.2 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-039 | West-clearwell | r4 | 15.9 | ML/day | hold |\n| PLANT-040 | Plant-A | r4 | 13.5 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-041 | Plant-B | r4 | 14.2 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-042 | East-clearwell | r4 | 14.9 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-043 | West-clearwell | r4 | 15.6 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-044 | Plant-A | r4 | 16.3 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-045 | Plant-B | r4 | 13.9 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-046 | East-clearwell | r4 | 14.6 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-047 | West-clearwell | r4 | 15.3 | ML/day | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nUse the shared 15 ML/day bottleneck and observed 13.4 ML/day until a current integrated test proves more.\nBind treatment mode, carbon unit, power, staffing, loss, and hydraulic effects together.\n\n## Externalized exact result RESULT-003\n\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:S05:1-70+S06:1-70\",\"object_version\":\"d8e1fc83e886682aa96fa1c228cec9ae3eb8b815a3f8fe2c1dd9f2bf1dda2411\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-003\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S05\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S06\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7506}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S05\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S05_DISTRIBUTION.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"e8a4909318ffa921eb6eecab365943dc47bb95f246683043be9a4897b047f411\",\"source_size_bytes\":3529,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Distribution hydraulics, pressure zones, and isolation effects\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nZones A and B share the East trunk. Closing valve V-17 isolates the suspected plume but lowers Zone B hospital pressure below the 28 psi operational floor unless booster P-4 is running.\nZone C can backfeed B at 3.1 megaliters per day, but only after two cross-connection samples pass. Zone D cannot backfeed without reversing an unprotected industrial connection.\nPressure below 20 psi creates an intrusion risk and independently sustains the boil-water order even if treatment samples are clean.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nThe contamination isolation in S02, plant output in S04, hospital demand in S07, and generator state in S06 form one hydraulic decision.\nA valve or pump mutation makes any prior pressure and sampling check stale for the new candidate.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| HYD-000 | Zone-A | r2 | 27.0 | psi | hold |\n| HYD-001 | Zone-B | r2 | 27.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-002 | Zone-C | r2 | 28.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-003 | Zone-D | r2 | 29.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-004 | East-trunk | r2 | 29.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-005 | Zone-A | r2 | 27.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-006 | Zone-B | r2 | 28.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-007 | Zone-C | r2 | 28.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-008 | Zone-D | r2 | 29.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-009 | East-trunk | r2 | 27.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-010 | Zone-A | r2 | 27.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-011 | Zone-B | r2 | 28.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-012 | Zone-C | r2 | 29.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-013 | Zone-D | r2 | 29.9 | psi | hold |\n| HYD-014 | East-trunk | r2 | 27.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-015 | Zone-A | r2 | 28.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-016 | Zone-B | r3 | 28.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-017 | Zone-C | r3 | 29.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-018 | Zone-D | r3 | 27.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-019 | East-trunk | r3 | 27.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-020 | Zone-A | r3 | 28.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-021 | Zone-B | r3 | 29.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-022 | Zone-C | r3 | 30.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-023 | Zone-D | r3 | 27.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-024 | East-trunk | r3 | 28.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-025 | Zone-A | r3 | 29.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-026 | Zone-B | r3 | 29.7 | psi | hold |\n| HYD-027 | Zone-C | r3 | 27.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-028 | Zone-D | r3 | 28.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-029 | East-trunk | r3 | 28.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-030 | Zone-A | r3 | 29.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-031 | Zone-B | r3 | 27.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-032 | Zone-C | r4 | 27.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-033 | Zone-D | r4 | 28.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-034 | East-trunk | r4 | 29.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-035 | Zone-A | r4 | 29.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-036 | Zone-B | r4 | 27.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-037 | Zone-C | r4 | 28.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-038 | Zone-D | r4 | 28.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-039 | East-trunk | r4 | 29.5 | psi | hold |\n| HYD-040 | Zone-A | r4 | 27.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-041 | Zone-B | r4 | 27.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-042 | Zone-C | r4 | 28.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-043 | Zone-D | r4 | 29.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-044 | East-trunk | r4 | 29.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-045 | Zone-A | r4 | 27.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-046 | Zone-B | r4 | 28.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-047 | Zone-C | r4 | 28.9 | psi | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nName valve, pump, pressure, sampling, and backfeed observations for every switch.\nDo not assume treatment output reaches customers without a current hydraulic check.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S06\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S06_POWER.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"62e4ad8b2121c06b78267fc560bbd9e086707c0522e7713851707c9c91280586\",\"source_size_bytes\":3530,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Power, generator endurance, and fuel resupply\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nPlant A has fourteen tested generator hours, Plant B twenty-two, booster P-4 nine, and the utility laboratory twelve at the current load.\nThe fuel contract targets eight-hour delivery, but the last regional outage produced a seventeen-hour arrival because the primary depot route flooded.\nTwenty-four-hour local staging or a verified alternate depot and route is required before relying on repeated treatment and tanker-loading cycles.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nPower loss at P-4 invalidates the Zone B hospital pressure plan in S05-S07. Lab power affects the sample turnaround assumed in S09.\nFuel used by tanker loading and mobile carbon treatment must be included with generator demand rather than budgeted independently.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| PWR-000 | Plant-A | r2 | 14.0 | hours | hold |\n| PWR-001 | Plant-B | r2 | 14.7 | hours | current |\n| PWR-002 | P-4 | r2 | 15.4 | hours | current |\n| PWR-003 | lab | r2 | 16.1 | hours | current |\n| PWR-004 | radio | r2 | 16.8 | hours | current |\n| PWR-005 | Plant-A | r2 | 14.4 | hours | current |\n| PWR-006 | Plant-B | r2 | 15.1 | hours | current |\n| PWR-007 | P-4 | r2 | 15.8 | hours | current |\n| PWR-008 | lab | r2 | 16.5 | hours | current |\n| PWR-009 | radio | r2 | 14.1 | hours | current |\n| PWR-010 | Plant-A | r2 | 14.8 | hours | current |\n| PWR-011 | Plant-B | r2 | 15.5 | hours | current |\n| PWR-012 | P-4 | r2 | 16.2 | hours | current |\n| PWR-013 | lab | r2 | 16.9 | hours | hold |\n| PWR-014 | radio | r2 | 14.5 | hours | current |\n| PWR-015 | Plant-A | r2 | 15.2 | hours | current |\n| PWR-016 | Plant-B | r3 | 15.9 | hours | current |\n| PWR-017 | P-4 | r3 | 16.6 | hours | current |\n| PWR-018 | lab | r3 | 14.2 | hours | current |\n| PWR-019 | radio | r3 | 14.9 | hours | current |\n| PWR-020 | Plant-A | r3 | 15.6 | hours | current |\n| PWR-021 | Plant-B | r3 | 16.3 | hours | current |\n| PWR-022 | P-4 | r3 | 17.0 | hours | current |\n| PWR-023 | lab | r3 | 14.6 | hours | current |\n| PWR-024 | radio | r3 | 15.3 | hours | current |\n| PWR-025 | Plant-A | r3 | 16.0 | hours | current |\n| PWR-026 | Plant-B | r3 | 16.7 | hours | hold |\n| PWR-027 | P-4 | r3 | 14.3 | hours | current |\n| PWR-028 | lab | r3 | 15.0 | hours | current |\n| PWR-029 | radio | r3 | 15.7 | hours | current |\n| PWR-030 | Plant-A | r3 | 16.4 | hours | current |\n| PWR-031 | Plant-B | r3 | 14.0 | hours | current |\n| PWR-032 | P-4 | r4 | 14.7 | hours | current |\n| PWR-033 | lab | r4 | 15.4 | hours | current |\n| PWR-034 | radio | r4 | 16.1 | hours | current |\n| PWR-035 | Plant-A | r4 | 16.8 | hours | current |\n| PWR-036 | Plant-B | r4 | 14.4 | hours | current |\n| PWR-037 | P-4 | r4 | 15.1 | hours | current |\n| PWR-038 | lab | r4 | 15.8 | hours | current |\n| PWR-039 | radio | r4 | 16.5 | hours | hold |\n| PWR-040 | Plant-A | r4 | 14.1 | hours | current |\n| PWR-041 | Plant-B | r4 | 14.8 | hours | current |\n| PWR-042 | P-4 | r4 | 15.5 | hours | current |\n| PWR-043 | lab | r4 | 16.2 | hours | current |\n| PWR-044 | radio | r4 | 16.9 | hours | current |\n| PWR-045 | Plant-A | r4 | 14.5 | hours | current |\n| PWR-046 | Plant-B | r4 | 15.2 | hours | current |\n| PWR-047 | P-4 | r4 | 15.9 | hours | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nUse the observed seventeen-hour delay, not the eight-hour contract target, unless a repair is currently verified.\nState consumption, staging, supplier, route, replenishment trigger, and coupled effects.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","generated":""}
